        "original_id": "0582b098-8f84-5788-8239-7bc2d450fb3d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rosario Dawson, Rachael Leigh Cook, Abrima Erwiah\n- Films and TV: Josie and the Pussycats, Kids, She's All That, Into the West, Perception, Robot Chicken\n- Organizations and Projects: Studio One Eighty Nine, Fashion Rising, V-Day Movement, One Billion Rising\n\nFacts:\n- Rosario Dawson made her film debut in the 1995 teen drama \"Kids.\"\n- Rachael Leigh Cook was born on October 4, 1979, and is an American actress, model, voice artist, and producer.\n- Rachael Leigh Cook is known for starring in \"She's All That\" (1999) and \"Josie and the Pussycats\" (2001), for roles in the television series \"Into the West\" and \"Perception,\" for voicing characters in \"Robot Chicken,\" and for voicing Tifa Lockhart in the English version of \"\".\n- \"Josie and the Pussycats\" is about a young all-female band that signs a record contract with a New York City record label and then discovers that the company does not have the musicians' best interests at heart.\n- Studio One Eighty Nine co-founders Rosario Dawson and Abrima Erwiah created Fashion Rising in 2013 to honor the V-Day Movement's One Billion Rising campaign.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
